From: Nerves ROCK Pi S maintainers <noreply@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: block: use host index for main device

The MMC core honors device-tree aliases for host numbering, but the block
driver independently assigns the first free mmcblk index as cards finish
probing. That makes mmcblk names nondeterministic even with aliases.

Reserve the aliased host index for each main card. Continue dynamically
allocating indices for eMMC boot and general-purpose subdevices.
---
 drivers/mmc/core/block.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/mmc/core/block.c b/drivers/mmc/core/block.c
--- a/drivers/mmc/core/block.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/core/block.c
@@ -2323,1 +2323,5 @@
-	devidx = ida_simple_get(&mmc_blk_ida, 0, max_devices, GFP_KERNEL);
+	if (!subname)
+		devidx = ida_simple_get(&mmc_blk_ida, card->host->index,
+				      card->host->index + 1, GFP_KERNEL);
+	else
+		devidx = ida_simple_get(&mmc_blk_ida, 0, max_devices, GFP_KERNEL);
--
